  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indian government has scheduled a special sitting of Parliament beginning November 30, 2026, to address a revised Delimitation Bill. This follows a failed attempt to pass similar legislation during the Monsoon session in April 2026. The new proposal aims to expand the number of seats in the Lok Sabha uniformly across all states, with current projections suggesting that the existing proportional seat distribution will remain unchanged until 2051. While the government seeks broad support for the initiative, regional and opposition parties have outlined conditions for their participation. The DMK has demanded that Tamil Nadu's representation remains unaffected, while the BJD and other factions have emphasized the need to protect their states' interests. Leadership from the NDA has met in Delhi to discuss the strategy for the upcoming legislative session amidst ongoing political negotiations.",
